From afef9fa7a8b42a8c5b1ec15857489937ea30187f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:11:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Thylacine Warp W-3 round-5 close: caps clamp + two
 soundness-argument corrections

F2 [P2]: the surface caps advertised maxImageExtent 8192x8192 while the
compositor's per-object registration budget is 64 MiB -- a caps-conformant
request (e.g. 8192x2049 BGRA8) drew the registration's keep-arm and leaked
one img handle per attempt; a resize-loop app could wedge all 16 slots.
maxImageExtent is now 4096x4096 = exactly the 64 MiB budget at 4 B/px, so
every caps-conformant single-image request fits (the server side
reclassifies the per-object cap refusal to E_NOMEM-after-taken in the same
close, so even a non-conformant request frees its handle).

F4 [P3]: the destroy-refused comment leaned on an unverified vkr
blob-holds-its-own-ref property; the actual guarantee is structural (the
only reachable refusal is a wedged transport, and the vkFreeMemory rides
the same dead conn) -- restated.

F5 [P3]: the stage-0 bracket header claimed the drain tails "every
vn_QueueSubmit*"; only vn_QueueSubmit2 has the vn_wsi_fence_wait tail, and
the drain holds because wsi_common's present submit routes through
QueueSubmit2 (wsi_queue_submit2_unordered) -- the dependency is now named
instead of overstated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi_thylacine.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi_thylacine.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi_thylacine.c
index 196c3f7..dfbf67d 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi_thylacine.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi_thylacine.c
@@ -35,9 +35,12 @@
  *
  * The I-40 stage-0 bracket: on the designed path venus itself drains the
  * queue before the vtable queue_present runs (vn_wsi_fence_wait at the tail
- * of every vn_QueueSubmit* detects the async-present tid and does the
- * empty-submit + fence + wait -- the vtest-class flow; our renderer reports
- * has_external_sync = has_implicit_fencing = false).  queue_present still
+ * of vn_QueueSubmit2 -- the entrypoint wsi_common's present submit uses,
+ * wsi_queue_submit2_unordered -> wsi->QueueSubmit2; the v1 vn_QueueSubmit
+ * has NO such tail, so the drain depends on that routing -- detects the
+ * async-present tid and does the empty-submit + fence + wait, the
+ * vtest-class flow; our renderer reports has_external_sync =
+ * has_implicit_fencing = false).  queue_present still
  * waits the per-image throttle fence itself so the bracket also holds under
  * VN_PERF=no_async_present, where that drain never runs.
  *
@@ -118,10 +121,17 @@ vn_thylacine_surface_get_capabilities(VkIcdSurfaceBase *surface,
 
    /* No intrinsic extent -- the surface is sized by the swapchain (the SDL
     * glue passes the tapestry surface geometry).  The compositor's
-    * registration gate re-validates against its own structural limits. */
+    * registration gate re-validates against its own structural limits.
+    *
+    * The extent ceiling is the REGISTRATION budget, not the dimension cap:
+    * a presentable's bytes (stride x height, 4 B/px) must fit the
+    * compositor's 64 MiB per-object bound, and advertising extents whose
+    * conformant request the registration then refuses would leak an img
+    * handle per attempt (round-5 F2).  4096 x 4096 x 4 = exactly 64 MiB,
+    * so every caps-conformant single-image request fits. */
    caps->currentExtent = (VkExtent2D){ -1, -1 };
    caps->minImageExtent = (VkExtent2D){ 1, 1 };
-   caps->maxImageExtent = (VkExtent2D){ 8192, 8192 };
+   caps->maxImageExtent = (VkExtent2D){ 4096, 4096 };
 
    caps->supportedTransforms = VK_SURFACE_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY_BIT_KHR;
    caps->currentTransform = VK_SURFACE_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY_BIT_KHR;
@@ -499,8 +509,13 @@ vn_thylacine_swapchain_destroy_image(struct vn_thylacine_swapchain *chain,
     * the display-safe teardown (unbind-before-unref server-side), and the
     * venus memory must outlive the presentable that names it.  A refused
     * unregister keeps the img handle marked renderer-side (bounded,
-    * ctx-death reaped) -- the memory free is still safe: the server's blob
-    * holds its own reference. */
+    * ctx-death reaped) -- and the memory free that follows is safe
+    * STRUCTURALLY: the only reachable refusal is a wedged transport (a
+    * live registered handle from the owning conn cannot draw E_NOENT), and
+    * on a wedged conn the vkFreeMemory rides the same dead conn and never
+    * reaches the host either; conn death then reaps both sides in the
+    * server's own display-safe order (round-5 F4 -- do not lean on any
+    * vkr blob-holds-its-own-ref property here; it is unverified). */
    if (image->registered) {
       struct vn_device *dev = vn_device_from_handle(chain->base.device);
       vn_renderer_thylacine_img_destroy(dev->renderer, image->img_handle);
